{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And in all that I have said to you, you shall guard.</b> To perform every positive commandment by way of warning — for every 'guarding' in the Torah is a warning in the place of a negative command (Menachot 36)." "<b>You shall not mention.</b> That one should not say to him, 'Keep something for me next to the idol of such-and-such,' or, 'Stand with me on the festival day of such-and-such an idol.' Another interpretation — <b>And in all that I have said to you, you shall guard, and the name of other elohim you shall not mention</b>: to teach you that idolatry is weighed against all the commandments combined (Horayot 8), and one who is heedful of it is as though he guards them all." "<b>It shall not be heard</b> from the gentile <b>upon your mouth.</b> That you should not enter a partnership with a gentile, so that he would swear to you by his idol — and you are found to be the cause of its being mentioned through you (Sanhedrin 67)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:08.234376678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}